  "text": "# What `serve/server.py` does\n\n`serve/server.py` is the HTTP front door of the Strata project (plan v0.3 P8). It is a Python `ThreadingHTTPServer` that exposes an OpenAI-compatible (`POST /v1/chat/completions`) and an Anthropic-compatible (`POST /v1/messages`) API on top of a token-id engine, plus metadata endpoints (`/v1/models`, `/models`, `/props`, `/slots`, `/health`, `/metrics`, `/mcp`, `/status`). Its responsibilities, in the order the file organizes them:\n\n1. **Engine abstraction.** An `Engine` protocol maps token ids in → token ids out. Two implementations exist:\n   - `MockEngine` replays a scripted completion as token ids so every API path (streaming, tools, cancellation, tests) can be exercised without a GPU.\n   - `StrataEngine` keeps one `strata --serve` process resident (weights, expert arena, VRAM tier load once) and speaks a line protocol over its stdin/stdout: `GEN <max_new> [sampling keys] <ids>` (or `GENI` for image requests) in, `T <id>` token",
